+## Changed in stage 2 (ecosystem/overlays/freeide/0002-gate.patch)
+
+- Default model provider is OpenVault FreeRoute at `NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL` + `/v1`
+  (default `http://127.0.0.1:5000`), model `openvault/auto`. Key comes from
+  `NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY`, issued by OpenVault. No key store was added.
+- No direct vendor endpoint is on by default. Upstream switched its Zen free tier on
+  with a public key; the fork needs the user's own key, auth login or config for Zen
+  like for every other vendor.
+- Shell, edit and webfetch POST `/api/crew/gate` on OpenVault before they act. The
+  body is ids only (kind, id, intent, parent_run_id, child_id, deficit): never a
+  command, path, diff, URL or skill body. Unreachable or not `allowed: true` stops
+  the tool with a visible error. There is no offline mode and no off switch.
+- Binary, platform package names, `--help` name, XDG config/data/cache/state
+  directories and user-facing command hints renamed to `freeide`.
+- Proof: `packages/opencode/test/netie/openvault-gate.test.ts` (fails on stage 1,
+  passes on stage 2).
+
+## Not done yet (stage 3)
+
+- Workspace package name, npm scope `@opencode-ai/*`, `OPENCODE_*` env vars,
+  project config file names (`opencode.json`, `.opencode/`), the desktop and
+  web packages, and the install script still carry upstream's name.
