-### Desktop App (BETA)
+```bash
+bun run --cwd packages/opencode dev            # same as `freeide` with the arguments that follow
+```
 
-FreeIDE is also available as a desktop application. Download directly from the [releases page](https://github.com/anomalyco/opencode/releases) or [opencode.ai/download](https://opencode.ai/download).
+### OpenVault
 
-| Platform              | Download                           |
-| --------------------- | ---------------------------------- |
-| macOS (Apple Silicon) | `opencode-desktop-mac-arm64.dmg`   |
-| macOS (Intel)         | `opencode-desktop-mac-x64.dmg`     |
-| Windows               | `opencode-desktop-windows-x64.exe` |
-| Linux                 | `.deb`, `.rpm`, or `.AppImage`     |
+FreeIDE holds no provider key. Models are served by OpenVault FreeRoute and every shell, edit and web fetch asks OpenVault's gate before it runs:
 
 ```bash
-# macOS (Homebrew)
-brew install --cask opencode-desktop
-# Windows (Scoop)
-scoop bucket add extras; scoop install extras/opencode-desktop
+export NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:5000   # default; FreeRoute is $NETIE_OPENVAULT_URL/v1
+export NETIE_OPENVAULT_KEY=ov_...                  # the key OpenVault issued to you
+freeide
 ```
 
-#### Installation Directory
+The default model is `openvault/auto` (FreeRoute's catalog pick). If OpenVault is unreachable, tools stop with an error that says so. There is no offline mode. Other providers come on only when you add their key with `freeide auth login` or in `opencode.json`; none is on by default.
 
-The install script respects the following priority order for the installation path:
+### Desktop App
 
-1. `$OPENCODE_INSTALL_DIR` - Custom installation directory
-2. `$XDG_BIN_DIR` - XDG Base Directory Specification compliant path
-3. `$HOME/bin` - Standard user binary directory (if it exists or can be created)
-4. `$HOME/.opencode/bin` - Default fallback
+Upstream ships a desktop application. FreeIDE does not ship one yet; the desktop package in this tree is unchanged upstream code and still carries upstream's name.
 
-```bash
-# Examples
-OPENCODE_INSTALL_DIR=/usr/local/bin curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/install | bash
-XDG_BIN_DIR=$HOME/.local/bin curl -fsSL https://opencode.ai/install | bash
-```
+#### Where FreeIDE keeps its files
+
+Config, data, cache and state live under the XDG directories as `freeide` (for example `~/.config/freeide`). Project-level config is still `opencode.json` or `.opencode/`, unchanged from upstream so existing projects keep working. The `OPENCODE_*` environment variables are unchanged too.
 
